"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1KCNW12WM1S0AY3D\",\"title\":\"Green Carbon - Kapadvanj Industrial Biochar — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"Green Carbon - Kapadvanj Industrial Biochar\",\"Green Carbon\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Project code\",\"A1JE\",\"Crediting period\",\"30 May 2026 to 30 May 2031\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"A1JE\",\"approval\":\"Expected 2026\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"11 May 2026\",\"Public Comment Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"10 Apr 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://green-carbon.co.jp\",\"t\":\"Green Carbon\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.3\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1KBMWD70R1S0VMYW\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-requirements\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KOmLuhU6yzCYYtUWPyQCw4aByEEJ7Q1-/view\",\"t\":\"VVB Policy\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1KBMWD70R1S0VMYW/prj_1KCNW12WM1S0AY3D/pjd_1KRB3QGKT1S0N6AR/public_comment_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1KBMWD70R1S0VMYW/prj_1KCNW12WM1S0AY3D/pjd_1KP85MYY61S0JT45/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nGreen Carbon - Kapadvanj Industrial Biochar\\nGreen Carbon\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nProject code\\nA1JE\\nCrediting period\\n30 May 2026 to 30 May 2031\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.3\\nSummary\\n\\nKapadvanj, Gujarat, India: The facility is designed to produce approximately 4,320 tonnes of biochar per year using cotton stalks and groundnut shells as feedstock, resulting in an estimated 10,009 tCO₂e of carbon credits annually (approximately 100,090 tCO₂e over a 10-year period).\\n\\nKapadvanj, Gujarat\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 19 Apr 2026\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2026\\nInitial documentation submission\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nAudit kick-off\\n\\nA Validation & Verification Body (VVB) officially commences the project validation and verification process. All VVBs are approved and appointed by Isometric based on the requirements outlined in the Isometric Standard and VVB Policy.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nSite visit\\nExpected 2026\\nApproval date\\nExpected 2026\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n11 May 2026\\tPublic Comment Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n10 Apr 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"